                        "entry_id": "7403ee1b-b756-3f7e-9e20-7f71160c8043",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "contumélieuses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9dbfdc96-cea7-3f53-bdaf-a7b070f35c71",
                        "entry_id": "7403ee1b-b756-3f7e-9e20-7f71160c8043",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui offense, qui outrage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Extrêmement rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b2c6aba-fc9a-443a-bd56-53a7c8fbf63d",
                                "sense_id": "9dbfdc96-cea7-3f53-bdaf-a7b070f35c71",
                                "text": "Je ne veux pas disputer de l'usage des serviteurs, à qui nous sommes si superbes, si cruels, si contumélieux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b695d73-34e2-4d0c-a249-a670e146e8f2",
                                "sense_id": "9dbfdc96-cea7-3f53-bdaf-a7b070f35c71",
                                "text": "Mais cette vindicte courrouça très âprement et survint un nombreux renfort de chicanes et démêlés contumélieux qui se déduisirent au plus grand dommage de l’Évêque grâce à la malignité rapace des officiers du Roi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6e09281-b68e-434f-8d24-bf7caa93baa8",
                                "sense_id": "9dbfdc96-cea7-3f53-bdaf-a7b070f35c71",
                                "text": "Or, des outrages par paroles, des actes ou des gestes contumélieux, non accompagnés de voies de fait, peuvent produire ce résultat, autant et plus même que les violences physiques. Les atteintes dirigées contre l'honneur et la réputation sont parfois autrement graves que ne le seraient des attaques corporelles; l'indignation qu'elles soulèvent est aussi plus vive et plus profonde."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bfd4bd81-63fc-4ffe-97da-bc34b9897b41",
                        "source_entry_id": "7403ee1b-b756-3f7e-9e20-7f71160c8043",
                        "source_sense_id": "9dbfdc96-cea7-3f53-bdaf-a7b070f35c71",
                        "target_lang_word": "contumelious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "contumelious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb375682-fddb-3814-b7bd-76c430ea66bb",
                                        "entry_id": "8036e56b-54c4-3dfd-ac30-af0a80d383e1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rudely contemptuous; showing contumely; exhibiting an insolent or disdainful attitude."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb97a71c-3087-4819-9ceb-481ab7b62599",
                                                "sense_id": "bb375682-fddb-3814-b7bd-76c430ea66bb",
                                                "text": "VVith ſcoffes and ſcornes, and contumelious taunts, / In open Market-place produc't they me, / To be a publique ſpectacle to all: / Here, ſayd they, is the Terror of the French, / The Scar-Crovv that affrights our Children ſo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b72d6400-522e-45c7-8d24-68832cd6aec0",
                                                "sense_id": "bb375682-fddb-3814-b7bd-76c430ea66bb",
                                                "text": "To sin against his law, is an high affront to his majesty; but to sin against his love and benefits is more contumelious to him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f10de58-cb2f-4a84-956e-6d72f8a762fd",
                                                "sense_id": "bb375682-fddb-3814-b7bd-76c430ea66bb",
                                                "text": "Such, and more contumelious, was the language of opposition in parliament, and of the pretended patriots in their private meetings, during the whole administration of sir Robert Walpole, who understood and pursued the true interests of his country, but, perhaps, without sufficiently attending to its honour."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e300c87-a5bb-40d0-bfc6-f982f54508cd",
                                                "sense_id": "bb375682-fddb-3814-b7bd-76c430ea66bb",
                                                "text": "The pad would not stay on Modestine’s back for half a moment. I returned it to its maker, with whom I had so contumelious a passage that the street outside was crowded from wall to wall with gossips looking on and listening."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cd47543-6c60-47fa-a236-146ff54c2303",
                                                "sense_id": "bb375682-fddb-3814-b7bd-76c430ea66bb",
                                                "text": "\"How now, you scullions and cullions: bring hither a pair of cow's hooves to out face this contumelious caitiff.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
